al (weather, computers). Concerns: teamwork/cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, known 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew, but difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, reliability, crew cooperation (positive atmosphere). Concerns: communication, development, egocentric.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, attention. Concerns: teamwork/leadership, attitude.\n\nWe need to start discussion. Perhaps pick candidate C as leading due to reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, despite communication issues. Or candidate B due to stress resilience and conscientiousness but teamwork concerns. Which is strongest overall? C seems strong on reliability, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty could affect cockpit communication. D has strong problem solving but arrogance. A has technical but organization issues.\n\nProbably C is best overall, but need to note concerns. Let's propose recommendation for Candidate C, but note need to address communication. Provide evidence. That is first contribution.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON vote: \"Candidate C\". Provide PUBLIC_MESSAGE with argument."}
